class_name Lore
## The documents scattered through the valley. Together they tell what happened to Polaris.

const NOTES := {
	"n_postcard": ["Unsent postcard", "Dear Mama,\n\nthe Christmas market is as pretty as you said. They have a carousel and a tree with a thousand lights.\n\nThe bus leaves at four. The driver says the tunnel is the only road out and the army has been checking papers there since Monday. Nobody will say why.\n\nThere was a green light under the ice on the lake last night. Everyone stood on the shore and watched, and nobody spoke.\n\nHome soon.\nYour Mirja"],
	"n_tove": ["Letter to Tove", "Tove,\n\nI have locked the lower gate of the Nordstern and I am not opening it again. The machine has been cutting on its own since the fourteenth. Nobody is in the cab. It stops when we come near and starts again when we leave.\n\nYou keep the key. If I keep it, I will go back down, and I do not think I should.\n\nThe bolt cutters and the rest of my things are in the office. Take what you want.\n\n— Arvid, shift foreman"],
	"n_ranger": ["Ranger's notebook", "From the tower, with the lake at your back:\n\nNORTH — the army's Fort Nordwacht at the head of the valley. The gate is shut. They do not answer the radio.\nNORTH-WEST — Polaris-7, the research station, behind the Eisklamm. The bridge fell in the quake. On foot you can climb down and up again with an ice pick, if your arms hold.\nEAST — the Nordstern mine under the Stollenkopf. Boarded up.\nSOUTH — the tunnel. That was the way out.\nBelow me — Eisgrund. Tove's people still fish.\n\nTwo shelters were dug in the sixties: B-2 by the fort and B-5 in the south meadows. B-5 was never locked, only stuck.\n\nThin ice shows dark. Remember that."],
	"n_bridge": ["Memo: emergency span", "TO: all Polaris-7 staff\n\nThe road bridge is closed until further notice. The centre section is at the bottom of the Eisklamm.\n\nThe army left us an emergency span. It stands upright at our end of the bridge. The lever in this hut lowers it. It carries one vehicle at a time, and it does not go back up.\n\nDo NOT lower it without the director's word. If it is down, anything can come across — in both directions."],
	"n_mine_log": ["Shift log, Nordstern mine", "11 Dec — K-9 cut 14 m in the lower chamber. Rock is warm to the hand. Halvorsen from the station came to take samples again.\n\n13 Dec — Lights failed twice. Meier says he heard the cutter run during the break. K-9 was parked. Key was in my pocket.\n\n14 Dec — K-9 running when we came on shift. Nobody aboard. Stopped when Meier shouted.\n\n15 Dec — It does not stop any more. It turns its lamps towards us.\n\n16 Dec — Pulled everyone out. Gate locked. Key goes to Tove in Eisgrund. Bolt cutters stay here in the office: the army has fenced half the valley and somebody will want them."],
	"n_mine_wall": ["Note in a tin", "If you found this room you pulled the boards off, so you are either one of us or desperate. Either way: take it.\n\nI hid here three days after the gate was locked. It scrapes at the rock all night. It is not digging for ore. It is digging DOWN, towards the lake.\n\n— Meier"],
	"n_mine_deep": ["Service tag: K-9 'Grabwurm'", "CONTINUOUS MINER K-9 — maintenance points\n\n1. HYDRAULIC LINES on both flanks, behind the yellow covers. A leak here stops the boom.\n2. COOLING GRILLE at the rear. Keep clear of dust. Overheats within a minute if blocked or damaged.\n3. CUTTER DRUM. Never approach from the front while it turns.\n4. LAMPS. The machine steers by them.\n\nDo not operate without a driver.\n\n(Scrawled underneath:) It does not need one."],
	"n_tunnel_order": ["Order 44", "FORT NORDWACHT — Maj. A. Voss\n\n1. The Polaris tunnel is to be closed at km 0.6. Charges are set. No vehicle, no person, no animal leaves the Senke until the Polaris matter is contained.\n2. Civilians who reach the portal are to be turned back to the village.\n3. Spare key for shelter B-2 remains in this service room. The armoury key stays in B-2. The Polaris-7 keycard stays in the armoury. Nobody carries more than one.\n\nThis order is not to be discussed."],
	"n_tunnel_driver": ["Page from a driver's log", "16:10 Left the market, 31 passengers.\n16:40 Stopped at the portal. Soldiers. Told to wait.\n17:05 Told to turn round. Cannot turn a bus in a tunnel. Said so.\n17:06 A bang from deeper in. Dust. The roof is coming down behind the lorry.\n\nGot them all out on foot. Left the bus. If anyone reads this: the service door on the left is jammed, not locked. A crowbar would do it."],
	"n_base_orders": ["Garrison orders", "FORT NORDWACHT\n\nGate is sealed from inside. Nobody opens it for anyone. If something heavy comes up the road at speed — shoot the driver, not the gate.\n\nThe east fence was patched with plain chain-link. I want it replaced before somebody notices.\n\nThe snow has drifted over the north-west corner again. Clear it. A child could walk in over it.\n\nB-2 holds the armoury key. The armoury holds the station keycard and the last of the good rifles.\n\n— Voss"],
	"n_base_diary": ["A private's diary", "He calls us his wolves now. He had red flags made.\n\nHalf the company walked out the night the tunnel went. They live in tents in the woods and take what they need from the village. The Major lets them. He says they are still his.\n\nI saw the thing on the lake through the tower glass. White, bigger than the carrier, and the ice bent under it but did not break. It looked up at the tower. I have not been on watch since.\n\nIf you read this and I am gone, I went over the drift at the north-west corner like the Major said a child could."],
	"n_bunker1": ["Radio log, shelter B-2", "POLARIS-7 → NORDWACHT\n\n02:14 'Core 31 is moving. Repeat, the sample is moving.'\n02:20 'Containment is holding. Halvorsen wants to continue.'\n03:02 'Lights under the lake ice. Same pulse as the aurora.'\n03:40 'It is out. It went through the wall. It is heading for the lake.'\n03:41 'Nordwacht, the bridge is gone. We are cut off.'\n04:15 'It is afraid of the flares. Tell them that. It is afraid of fire.'\n\nNo further traffic."],
	"n_bunker2": ["Shelter B-5: list on the wall", "CIVIL SHELTER B-5 — capacity 12\n\nStores: tinned food, water, blankets, lamp oil, first aid.\nTake what you need. Leave what you can.\n\nPeople who passed through:\n  the Lindqvists (4) — gone to Eisgrund\n  Otto from the cable car — back to the village\n  two students from the station — went north to find the army. Did not come back.\n\nIf the door sticks, lean on it with iron. It always has."],
	"n_station_log": ["Research log, Dr. I. Halvorsen", "POLARIS-7\n\nThe signal comes from under the glacier. It pulses with the aurora — or the aurora pulses with it.\n\nThe mine gave us access from below. Core 31 came up from 240 m: ice that is not ice. It stays cold in a warm room. It grows towards the lamp.\n\nWe put it in tank C. In four days it had a spine.\n\nI asked the Major for more time. He gave me a fence, a blown tunnel and a soldier at my door.\n\nIf it wakes fully I do not think walls are the right idea."],
	"n_station_beast": ["Field notes: 'the white one'", "What we know, written fast:\n\n— The plates on its back and head turn bullets. Do not waste them there.\n— The JOINTS between the plates glow when it breathes. Aim there.\n— The belly is soft. You only see it when it rears.\n— It hates fire. A flare makes it turn away for a few seconds.\n— It will not cross dark ice. It knows what holds it and what does not. A heavy vehicle does not know.\n— It hunts by sound first.\n\nIt came from the lake and it goes back to the lake."],
	"n_cordon_order": ["Cordon standing order", "SPERRE SÜD — Lt. H. Maurer\n\nThe tunnel is shut and stays shut. Our orders came from the same desk as Order 44: nothing leaves the Senke.\n\nNobody told us what to do when nothing came to relieve us either. The road south of Grauwasser is under forty metres of slide. The radio at Hochfunk has been dead since the storm. We are a cordon around a cordon.\n\nIf you are reading this and you came THROUGH the tunnel: the town is two kilometres down the road. Tell them the Senke is alive. Do not tell them what is in the lake."],
	"n_gw_notice": ["Town notice, Grauwasser", "BY ORDER OF THE COUNCIL\n\n1. Bread is rationed. Fuel is rationed. Bullets are not, and that tells you how things stand.\n2. The sawmill is in the hands of Hauptmann Reiss and his Red Flags. Nobody goes east of the junction alone.\n3. Dr. Brandt holds surgery in the Gasthof every morning.\n4. Anyone who can make the Hochfunk mast speak again will be fed for life.\n\n— R. Halden, Mayor"],
	"n_mill_ledger": ["Reiss's ledger", "Taken this week: 40 l diesel, 2 pigs, the doctor's morphine.\n\nFalk thinks holding the fort means holding the valley. He is wrong. Whoever holds the only saw, the only fuel and the only road holds Grauwasser, and Grauwasser is the door to everything else.\n\nThe relay fuse from the mast is in the field hospital, in the surgeon's case. As long as the mast is dumb, nobody outside knows there is anything here to take back.\n\nIf Falk is dead, good. One colonel fewer."],
	"n_camp_triage": ["Triage book, Feldlazarett 3", "Day 1 — 60 beds, 9 staff. Frostbite, two gunshot.\nDay 4 — The ones from the lake shore do not warm up. Core temperature 31 and falling, and they are walking about.\nDay 6 — Evacuation flight cancelled: rotor hub cracked on landing. The spare is on the supply sled. The sled went into the quarry road in the white-out.\nDay 7 — Something is living in the Steinbruch. The dogs will not go near it.\nDay 9 — We are leaving on foot for the cordon. I took the relay fuse out of the mast set so that Reiss cannot sell this valley over the air. It is in my case. Forgive me. — Stabsarzt K. Lindqvist"],
	"n_mast_log": ["Hochfunk log", "02:10 — carrier lost. Relay fuse gone from the rack. Somebody has been in here.\n02:40 — generator dry.\n\nFor whoever gets this set working: the regional net listens on 3 1 8 6 at the top of every hour. Say who you are, say how many, say Grauwasser. Then listen. — L."],
	"n_strip_manifest": ["Hangar chalk board", "SEA KING 'GRETE'\n\nMain rotor hub — CRACKED. Spare ordered, never arrived.\nFuel — 40 l short of a flight to Kiruna.\nSeats — four, with the stretcher out.\n\nFour seats. Two thousand people. I have stopped answering the door. — Brandt"],
	"n_quarry_den": ["Blood-stained map", "Supply sled went over the quarry lip here (X). Crates are scattered down the east wall.\n\nDo not go down. The big grey one took Persson and it did not eat him. It just stood on him until he stopped moving, and the frost came out of its mouth.\n\nThe wolves here have ice in their coats that does not melt in the hand."],
	"n_farm_letter": ["Letter on the kitchen table", "Oda,\n\nI have taken the tractor and the two youngest to town. The Red Flags came for the diesel again and this time they looked at the barn for a long while.\n\nThe cellar key is where your mother kept it. There is a rifle down there that your grandfather never handed in. If you stay, stay armed.\n\n— Per"],
}
